{{APP_DISPLAY}} - Windows deployment

Run the application:
  Double-click "Run {{APP_DISPLAY}}.bat".

The first run prepares pinned uv, managed Python {{PYTHON_VERSION}}, and an isolated
environment for this Windows user beneath LocalAppData. Later launches use a fast
fingerprint check and normally open immediately.

Repair:
  Double-click "Repair {{APP_DISPLAY}} Environment.bat".

Diagnostics:
  Double-click "Diagnose {{APP_DISPLAY}}.bat".

This deployment does not request administrator privileges, modify PATH, alter system
Python, or use PowerShell. Detailed logs are stored beneath:
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\PythonDeploymentBuilder\apps\{{APP_ID}}\logs

If the GUI exits during startup, an application-launch-failure log is written there
and its most recent path is included by Diagnose.

Bootstrap mode: {{BOOTSTRAP_MODE}}
System certificate store for uv: {{SYSTEM_CERTS_DESCRIPTION}}

Generating this kit verifies its structure and dependency lock. Fresh-workstation GUI
and runtime acceptance testing remains a separate validation step.

Fresh Windows Standard User checklist:
  1. Extract the complete ZIP beneath your user profile.
  2. Double-click "Run {{APP_DISPLAY}}.bat".
  3. Confirm setup completes without elevation and the GUI opens.
  4. Confirm application resources, file browsing, and output paths work.
  5. Confirm the GUI can open without an API key; configure a session key only if needed.
  6. Close the application and launch it again to confirm the fast path.
  7. Run Diagnose and Repair once as directed by the developer test plan.

The deployment still needs permitted network access for managed Python and locked
packages unless those artifacts are already cached or supplied by a future offline bundle.
